{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-lichnerowicz-q-correction","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:lichnerowicz-q-correction","kind":"remark","title":"The $\\tfrac14\\mathrm{Sc}_q$ correction term and its vanishing on the Bring background","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-lichnerowicz","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-laplacian-expansion","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-categorical-reeb-brings"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-lichnerowicz","tags":["lichnerowicz","q-laplacian","q-anomaly","scalar-curvature"],"text":"lichnerowicz-q-correction.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:lichnerowicz-q-correction\"></a><p>The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-scalar curvature <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Sc}_q = R + O(\\hbar_q)</code> encodes both the classical scalar curvature and the anomaly contribution from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2 \\neq 0</code>. The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">O(\\hbar_q)</code> correction adds a contact-curvature term on a non-flat substrate. On the contact-flat Bring background, both contributions vanish, yielding <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_\\nabla^q = \\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla^2</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/lichnerowicz-q-correction.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.17.11","page":"b/rem-lichnerowicz-q-correction","qa":{"counts":{"pass":58,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
